{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Refrain from anger:</b> If he provokes you because he is wealthy and you are not like him, do not let your anger burn to do him harm. And according to the interpretation of \"do not fret,\" do not mingle with him to show him affection and kindness while in your heart you intend only to do him harm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:52.925167177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}